+## Untested scope
+- Seam reviewer, B2 and B1 producer: `PersistentServiceClient` still registers `service_session_v2` (`src/client/service.rs:560`) and `result_matches` (`:906`) has no arm for any v3 result, while herdr-graph's real adapter is built on that client (`herdr-graph/src/threads/adapter.rs:1,146,179`); the only v3 path is the one `docs/programmatic-service-client.md` line 40 documents, where the caller frames `ServiceWireRequest` on its own socket with its own operation keys, and only tests do that today, so the seam reviewer should decide whether this counts as a supported producer for "graph undo reverses it"; this path leaves the cluster and `src/client/service.rs` is outside the diff, so this review does not call the row undelivered.
+- Seam reviewer, epic scope: beads ht-ma6i.1 (G2), ht-ma6i.4 (G5) and ht-ma6i.11 (integration sweep) are open at this head and no `decide_shell_continuity` exists in `src/`, only the schema tables and a table list entry in `src/service/kicks.rs`; G2 and G5 are not baseline rows but are in the epic's goal, and this cluster holds no shell-continuity provenance constant because that bead has not landed.
+- The wire spelling `"final"` of `SeatRetirementState::Final` is not pinned: `tests/cli/launch.rs:1409` pins `"reversible"` and absence, while the store and human tests compare the enum value, so a rename would pass them.
+- `ServiceSessionLevel::required_by` has a unit assertion only for `Send` and the five v3 operations; the V1 arms are covered indirectly by the daemon session test's v1 flow, and each arm is forced by the exhaustive match but its chosen level is not individually pinned.
+- This review ran no cargo tests on the cluster; the tests it cites were read at the head SHA and their results come from the owners' reports and the caller's later full-suite run.
+
+## Deferred OK
+- `seat inspect` text shows no conflict and no `bound_by` (`tests/protocol/output.rs` pins this): spec 4.7 defines only the key line, spec 4.2's conflict display is met in `--json`, and an operator reading text output has to ask for `--json` to see a standing conflict.
+- Spec 4.7's sizes (`4 bytes plus the key and owner`, `9 bytes more than retired`) and its bare `retired (reversible)` differ from the shipped `key KEY OWNER` (6 bytes plus) and `state: retired (reversible)` (28 bytes); the code comments state the true sizes and the spec text should be corrected in a post-implementation note.
+- `KEY_CONFLICT_CAUSE` classifies a conflict by a string prefix on `ApiError.detail` rather than a typed code, as recorded for ht-ma6i.6; the constant is shared with the store's formatter, so the two cannot drift, but a typed code would be sturdier.
+- `docs/programmatic-service-client.md` line 53 lists `InvalidCursor` and `InvalidBudget` for `ContinuityAlerts`, while the task 6 record says an invalid page request returns `InvalidRequest`; this is the doc drift already recorded for ht-ma6i.9, and it is still present at this head.
+- `ContinuityAlerts` has no resume cursor, so a poller rereads up to 256 rows and skips ordinals it has seen; the doc states this, and adding one would be a later protocol change.
